module.exports={
 en:{
  answer:'Outbound agencies usually charge a retainer, a fee per defined meeting, or a hybrid. Compare the full commitment, included work and billing trigger before comparing prices. Beespoke manages cold email and/or LinkedIn for USD 1,500 per month, or EUR 1,500 per month in Europe, with a three-month minimum and no per-meeting fee. Third-party costs are separate unless the written scope includes them; cold calling is quoted separately.',
  own:'Beespoke’s managed cold email and/or LinkedIn service costs USD 1,500 per month, or EUR 1,500 per month in Europe, with a three-month minimum and no per-meeting fee. The minimum service commitment is therefore USD 4,500 or EUR 4,500 before separate third-party costs and any applicable taxes. These are regional prices, not currency conversions.',
  position:'The founder-led service covers targeting, research, individual messaging, authorized campaign setup, replies, agreed qualification and calendar coordination. Your team approves the target lists and fit, authorizes execution, and handles discovery, proposals and closing. Cold calling is outside the base plan and is quoted by market; required software and data are separate unless included in writing.',
  startup:['How much does it cost to start outbound? Build a 90-day budget','Start with a written scope and a funding period. Separate the amount owed under the contract from the date you hope to see useful evidence. A review after a month does not cancel a three-month commitment.',['Budget item','What to include'],[['Service fees','All fees owed during the evaluation period, including any longer minimum term.'],['Tools and data','Licenses, inboxes, domains, verification and data charges not already included.'],['Internal work','List approval, product questions, discovery and follow-up hours at your fully loaded hourly cost.'],['One-time charges','Only setup or integration charges actually quoted; state their refund and ownership terms.'],['Currency and tax','One stated billing currency; separate applicable tax. Do not silently convert quotes.']],'Wholly fictional example, not a Beespoke quote or a forecast: 3 × (2,000 service + 300 tools/data + 400 internal time) + 500 setup = 8,600 in one billing currency, before tax. Every input is invented. Replace it with your quote; this example establishes no setup fee for Beespoke.'],
  invoice:['Check the invoice unit, not just the monthly headline','A calendar month and four weeks are different billing periods. This fictional comparison has identical scope and no extras.',['Fictional billing unit','Annual invoices','Annual service total'],[['2,000 per calendar month','12','24,000'],['2,000 every four weeks','13 over 52 weeks','26,000']],'The second costs 2,000 more over 52 weeks despite the same headline number. Actual contracts may prorate partial periods or use different renewal dates. Check the invoice schedule, notice deadline, remaining balance and asset export before signing.'],
  modelNote:'Other quotes may bill by contact, dedicated rep, pod, hour, one-time system build or closed revenue. These are not interchangeable with managed campaign delivery. For commission, define collected versus contracted revenue, attribution, refunds and any post-contract tail. For a build-only project, identify who runs messages and replies after handover. A billing model alone does not guarantee quality or transfer all risk.',
  toolTitle:'Model one cohort before funding the next',toolIntro:'Enter the total cost and qualified meetings held from the same evaluation period. The model estimates first-year gross profit from customers associated with that cohort. It does not estimate monthly profit, cash payback or a complete customer acquisition cost.',
  worked:'Wholly fictional worked example: 3,000 total program cost; 12 qualified meetings held; 25% become opportunities; 20% of opportunities become customers; 20,000 first-year revenue per customer; 60% gross margin. That models 0.60 customers, 7,200 first-year gross profit and 4,200 after the entered program cost: 2.40× gross-profit/cost, or 140% surplus/cost. At these assumptions, five whole qualified meetings would cover the entered cost.',
  downside:'Downside check: halve the qualified meetings to six, leaving other assumptions unchanged. Modeled customers fall to 0.30, first-year gross profit to 3,600 and surplus to 600. At zero meetings, gross profit is zero and the full 3,000 program cost remains. Fractional modeled customers are an expected value across comparable cohorts, not an actual part-customer or a booking promise.',
  cash:'A first-year contract value is not cash available today. Collection dates, delivery costs, churn, cancellations and later sales work can change the economics. Use observed revenue and margin where available, allow the same outcome follow-up time for each cohort, and keep pending opportunities separate. Do not fund a program you cannot carry while waiting for payment.',
  toolSummary:'Optional calculator: use your own assumptions',unitLabel:'Scenario currency',periodLabel:'Evaluation period',periodOptions:['One month','90 days'],labels:['Total program cost for the period','Qualified meetings held in the period','Held meeting → accepted opportunity (%)','Accepted opportunity → customer (%)','First-year revenue per customer','Gross margin (%)'],outputs:['Modeled customers from this cohort','Modeled first-year gross profit','Gross profit less entered program cost','Gross profit ÷ entered cost','Surplus ÷ entered cost','Whole qualified meetings needed'],inputHelp:'Include service fees, separate tools/data, setup allocated to this period and internal work once. Rates must be between 0 and 100; meetings must be whole numbers. Unknown inputs are blank, not zero.',unitHelp:'Changing the period or currency relabels your scenario; it does not multiply costs, convert amounts or change Beespoke’s regional prices. Keep every monetary input in one currency.',empty:'Enter all six assumptions, or load the fictional example.',invalid:'Complete every field with valid non-negative numbers. Use whole meetings and percentages from 0 to 100.',overflow:'These values exceed the calculator’s numerical range. Use smaller, meaningful assumptions.',valid:'Scenario only. Check the assumptions and cash timing before making a decision.',undefined:'Undefined',load:'Load fictional example',reset:'Clear assumptions',noscript:'The worked calculations above remain readable without JavaScript. The optional calculator needs JavaScript. Entries are not sent or saved.',
  events:['Reconcile the billable event before calculating unit cost','Wholly fictional record: six visible rows represent five original bookings, because A appears twice. Use the original booking ID, not the number of calendar rows.',['Original booking','Status at the cutoff','Count it as'],[['A','Held, fits criteria, accepted by sales','1 qualified held meeting; 1 opportunity'],['B','Held and fits criteria; no opportunity yet','1 qualified held meeting; 0 accepted opportunities'],['C','No-show','0 held meetings'],['D','Held, outside agreed target','0 qualified held meetings'],['E','Rescheduled beyond the cutoff','Pending; 0 held meetings at this cutoff'],['A again','Duplicate export row','No new booking, meeting or opportunity']],'There are two qualified meetings held and one accepted opportunity at this cutoff. A contract may invoice a different event; reconcile it to the written definition and dispute rules. A reschedule is not a new original booking. With zero accepted opportunities, cost per accepted opportunity is undefined, not zero.'],
  replyTitle:'Agree who answers, qualifies and hands over',replyText:'For Beespoke, targeting, research, messages, follow-up, replies, agreed qualification and calendar coordination are part of the managed cold email and/or LinkedIn service. Your team approves lists and fit and authorizes execution; it retains product decisions, discovery, proposals and closing. Put coverage hours, escalation for technical questions, opt-out handling, CRM access and the agreed qualification definition in the written scope. There is no per-meeting fee; third-party costs and separately quoted calling remain distinct.',
  sourceNote:'The provider source list below is the historical July 20, 2026 snapshot, retained rather than presented as current rate cards. Commercial offers can change. This November 13 revision corrects Beespoke’s approved scope and improves the planning method; it adds no new provider rates, guarantees or market averages. Beespoke sells the managed service described here, so this is a buyer guide with a publisher interest, not an independent market survey.',
  faqs:[['What is Beespoke’s minimum outbound commitment?','The service is USD 1,500 per month, or EUR 1,500 per month in Europe, for a three-month minimum: USD 4,500 or EUR 4,500 in service fees. Required third-party costs and applicable taxes are separate unless included in writing. Cold calling is separately quoted; there is no per-meeting fee.'],['Does first-year gross profit show when the campaign pays back in cash?','No. The calculator models first-year gross profit from one cohort of customers, then subtracts the entered program cost. Payment timing, churn, delivery, taxes and other acquisition costs may differ. It is not monthly profit, cash payback or complete CAC.'],['What if the inputs or opportunity count are unknown?','Leave unknown assumptions blank; the calculator withholds results until all six inputs are valid. Zero is a real assumption, not a substitute for missing evidence. Cost per opportunity is undefined when no opportunities have been accepted.']],updated:'Updated November 13, 2026'
 }
};
